                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 208,
                            "last_played": 1751045169
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b] Choose your co-op partner wisely. [/b]\n\nI've played this game twice with two completely different people, and the experience couldn't have been more different.\n\nThe first time, I played with someone who was honestly impossible to play with. They never even wanted to know what was on my screen. They never asked me what I was seeing and just kept trying to solve every puzzle on their own, even though the whole point is that you literally can't solve them without communicating with each other. Sometimes they would even ask me to just send them screenshots of my screen instead of actually discussing the puzzle with me. Every new puzzle felt more like torture than a fun co-op experience. We got stuck on the second level and eventually stopped playing. We don't even talk anymore.\n\nA couple of years later, I played the game again with someone else, and it was a completely different experience. We actually communicated, discussed what we were seeing, took turns coming up with ideas, helped each other whenever one of us got stuck, and trusted each other. We ended up playing through all three games in the series and didn't have a single argument.\n\nThe same game can either feel like torture or be an amazing experience depending entirely on who you're playing with.",
